## Control Plane

This repository contains orchestration metadata only:

- `config.yml` — repository topology, environment branches, Job Template names,
  and optional shared references for tenant-bound Dispatchers
- `tenants.yml` — tenant registry; tenants use the shared Dispatcher by default
  and may optionally select a central tenant-bound Dispatcher
- `naming-rules.yml.sample` — inert comprehensive naming-policy example covering cataloged `naming_supported` types (rename, adapt, and uncomment as `naming-rules.yml` to activate; never auto-activates)

Do not place AAP desired-state resource YAML in this repository. Use the
separate platform desired-state repository and its environment branches.
{% else %}
## Usage

Place YAML files in the `base/` directory using the appropriate resource type
subdirectory (e.g., `base/projects/`, `base/templates/`). Environment-specific
overrides go in `<env>/` directories (e.g., `dev/`, `prd/`).

The pipeline routes this repository to its configured tenant-bound Dispatcher,
or to the shared Dispatcher when no dedicated JT is configured.

Use the
[AAP CasC Resource Catalog]({{ _engine_repo_url }}{{ _engine_blob_path }}main/docs/RESOURCE_CATALOG.md)
for supported resource keys, complete YAML examples, parameter references, and
merge behavior.

### Example

```yaml
---
{{ repo.casc_key | default('aap_organizations') }}:
  - name: example-resource
    description: Replace with your actual configuration
```
{% endif %}

## CI/CD Pipeline

This repository includes a thin CI/CD caller that triggers the platform's
shared CasC pipeline on push and pull request events. The pipeline validates
YAML files and triggers the dispatcher Job Template in AAP.

